From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sysretq0 <sysretq0@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:35:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: mediatek: Configure MT6789 CONN power domain for CONNSYS

MediaTek MT6789's integrated CONNSYS connectivity subsystem
(mediatek,mt6789-consys) requires its SCPSYS power domain
(MT6789_POWER_DOMAIN_CONN) to remain powered off across driver attach
until the CONNSYS driver has configured EMI address remapping, enabled
the CCIF4 AP clock, and brought up the VCN PMIC rails, after which it
explicitly powers CONN on via pm_runtime_get_sync() and marks the device
as a wakeup source.

1. Skip automatic attach-time power-on in genpd_dev_pm_attach() for
   mediatek,mt6789-consys so CONN stays off until runtime-resumed.
2. Add MTK_SCPD_ACTIVE_WAKEUP to MT6789_POWER_DOMAIN_CONN so genpd
   keeps CONN MTCMOS active across s2idle while Wi-Fi/CONNSYS is live.

Signed-off-by: sysretq0 <sysretq0@proton.me>
---
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/core.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/core.c
@@ -3565,6 +3565,8 @@
  */
 int genpd_dev_pm_attach(struct device *dev)
 {
+	bool power_on = true;
+
 	if (!dev->of_node)
 		return 0;
 
@@ -3576,7 +3578,10 @@
 				       "#power-domain-cells") != 1)
 		return 0;
 
-	return __genpd_dev_pm_attach(dev, dev, 0, 1, true);
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "mediatek,mt6789-consys"))
+		power_on = false;
+
+	return __genpd_dev_pm_attach(dev, dev, 0, 1, power_on);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(genpd_dev_pm_attach);
 
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mt6789-pm-domains.h
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/mediatek/mt6789-pm-domains.h
@@ -109,7 +109,8 @@
 					MT6789_TOP_AXI_PROT_EN_1_CLR,
 					MT6789_TOP_AXI_PROT_EN_1_STA1),
 		},
-		.caps = MTK_SCPD_KEEP_DEFAULT_OFF,
+		.caps = MTK_SCPD_KEEP_DEFAULT_OFF |
+			MTK_SCPD_ACTIVE_WAKEUP,
 	},
 	[MT6789_POWER_DOMAIN_MFG0] = {
 		.name = "mfg0",
